11
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Focus is a 2015 American crime comedy-drama film written and
directed by Glenn Ficarra and John Requa.

12
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
It stars Will Smith as a seasoned con artist who becomes romantically
involved with an aspiring grifter, played by Margot Robbie.

13
01:02:02,727 --> 01:02:08,727
Rodrigo Santoro, Gerald McRaney, and Adrian Martinez appear in supporting roles.

14
01:06:49,090 --> 01:06:55,090
The screenplay was developed by Ficarra and Requa, who
previously collaborated on Crazy, Stupid, Love (2011).

15
01:11:35,454 --> 01:11:41,454
Filming took place in New Orleans, Buenos Aires, and New
York City between September and December 2013.

16
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
The film features themes of deception, trust, and manipulation
within the world of high-stakes con artistry.

17
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
Focus premiered at the TCL Chinese Theatre on February 24, 2015, and was
theatrically released in the United States on February 27 by Warner Bros.

18
01:25:54,545 --> 01:26:00,545
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with praise for the
chemistry between Smith and Robbie but criticism for its plot.

19
01:30:40,909 --> 01:30:46,909
It emerged as a box office success, grossing $158.8 million
worldwide against a production budget of $50 million.

20
01:35:27,272 --> 01:35:33,272
The film explores themes of seduction, con man, illusion, deception, rivalry.

21
01:40:13,636 --> 01:40:19,636
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
